+# Homepage asset integrity
+
+The SHA-384 digests in `index.html` were computed at implementation time from the exact downloaded asset bytes, not in the visitor’s browser. The JavaScript, stylesheet, and font URLs pin npm package versions. Public CDN responses must retain `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.
+
+The Unsplash stock photo URLs pin photo IDs, JPEG format, crop dimensions, and quality, but the image service does not guarantee immutable bytes. Changed responses intentionally fail integrity checks; review replacements and update the digests explicitly. Do not restore `auto=format`, which can produce different bytes across clients.
+
+`images/*.jpg` are reviewed local snapshots of those photo responses for browsers without CSS URL request-modifier support. They are served from the site origin. Supporting browsers use only the integrity-checked remote declaration; a failed integrity check must not retry an unchecked remote URL. Browsers without the font modifiers use Georgia/serif.
+
+To update an asset, download and review the replacement, compute `openssl dgst -sha384 -binary <file> | openssl base64 -A`, and replace the matching `sha384-` value. Refresh the corresponding local photo snapshot when changing an image. Keep `cross-origin(anonymous)` and `referrer-policy(no-referrer)` inside CSS `url()`, and `crossorigin="anonymous"` and `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"` on HTML CDN links/scripts.
